To ensure effective ventilation, one should avoid obstructions in ducts or vents, overcrowding spaces which hampers air circulation, and the use of materials or substances that emit harmful gases or pollutants. Blocking airways can significantly reduce airflow, while poor space planning and hazardous substances can compromise indoor air quality. Thus, maintaining clear pathways for air movement and minimizing pollutant sources are crucial for effective ventilation.
