When performing chest compressions on an infant, first ensure the scene is safe and call for emergency medical services if not already done. Position the infant on their back and ensure the airway is clear by gently tilting the head back. Place two fingers on the center of the infant's chest just below the nipple line and press down about 1.5 inches deep at a rate of 100-120 compressions per minute, allowing the chest to fully recoil between compressions.

