When performing rescue breathing, you should provide one breath every 5 to 6 seconds for an adult, which translates to about 10 to 12 breaths per minute. This frequency may vary slightly based on the age and condition of the patient. It's crucial to ensure that each breath lasts about one second and makes the chest visibly rise.

